          "evidence": "The vertex for 2012 is at a vertical position corresponding to ~1200, while the vertex for 2023 is at a vertical position corresponding to ~3200. The 2023 point is physically higher on the page.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "The y-axis is labeled 'Emergency department visits' and has tick labels 0, 800, 1600, 2400, and 3200 in ascending order from bottom to top.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "3": {
          "evidence": "The x-axis is labeled 'Year' and has tick marks for every year from 2012 to 2023.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "1. The plotted line encodes emergency department visits by year, with higher vertical position corresponding to larger values. 2. A later endpoint plotted higher than the earlier endpoint indicates overall utilization growth. 3. Endpoint comparison is an appropriate measure of the review-period overall pattern.",
        "evidence": "Condition 1 is established by the axis labels. Condition 2 is established by the fact that the 2023 point (~3200) is higher than the 2012 point (~1200). Condition 3 is supported by the task instruction to assess the 'overall utilization pattern over the review period', where the endpoints represent the start and end of that period.",
